\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Localized complementarity across the ZeBRA risk axis.} (a) Directional nested-model likelihood-ratio statistics in clinically relevant control-FPR bands. (b) Overlapping moving windows show substantial residual \textit  {MUC5B} information through intermediate and high ZeBRA percentiles, followed by a sharp rise of the residual ZeBRA contribution in the extreme clinical-risk tail. (c) Within the same score axis, observed FILD/FILA prevalence is consistently higher among \textit  {MUC5B} T-carriers than non-carriers. (d) Local adjusted odds ratios provide an effect-size view of the same transition. Moving windows overlap and are used for descriptive localization rather than as independent hypothesis tests; no nominal significance threshold is shown.}}{9}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:local-information}{{3}{9}{\textbf {Localized complementarity across the ZeBRA risk axis.} (a) Directional nested-model likelihood-ratio statistics in clinically relevant control-FPR bands. (b) Overlapping moving windows show substantial residual \textit {MUC5B} information through intermediate and high ZeBRA percentiles, followed by a sharp rise of the residual ZeBRA contribution in the extreme clinical-risk tail. (c) Within the same score axis, observed FILD/FILA prevalence is consistently higher among \textit {MUC5B} T-carriers than non-carriers. (d) Local adjusted odds ratios provide an effect-size view of the same transition. Moving windows overlap and are used for descriptive localization rather than as independent hypothesis tests; no nominal significance threshold is shown}{figure.3}{}}
